# The image takes only what installs and runs the engine, so files Git ignores in a working
# tree (credentials, benchmark output, local environments) never reach it. It has no .git:
# the build writes REVISION from its build argument instead.
*
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES
!python
!scripts
!environments
!cookbook
!docker

# Within those, no hidden files and nothing else .gitignore excludes.
**/.*
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*$py.class
**/*.dist-info
**/*.egg-info
**/*.json
**/*.jsonl
**/*.nsys-rep
**/*.ncu-rep
**/build
**/dist
**/*.tar.gz
**/venv
**/env
**/htmlcov
